## Context
The command sections of spec-erg-v1.md (validate rules, check semantics, ready
query, close atomicity, archive preconditions, migrate table) are implementation
documentation that belongs in Go doc comments. Each cmdXxx function currently
has a minimal one-line comment or none at all. Moving the spec prose into doc
comments makes the source self-documenting, enables go doc, and is the
foundation for per-command --help (0090) and --help --all (0091).

Go 1.19+ supports `// # Section` headers and lists in doc comments, rendering
clean markdown output via go doc.

## Actions
1. For each command function (cmdValidate, cmdCheck, cmdReady, cmdClose,
   cmdArchive, cmdMigrate, cmdInit, cmdNew, cmdLog, cmdNextID, cmdVersion,
   cmdUpdate), write a full doc comment containing:
   - One-line summary (existing usage signature)
   - Full description taken from the corresponding spec section
   - Use `// # Header` and `//  - list` for structure (Go 1.19 doc syntax)
2. For format constants (RequiredHeaders, AllowedTags, log line grammar), add
   doc comments with the spec table content — these don't exist yet as named
   constants; extract them from validate.go literals first.
3. Verify `go doc ./src/go/` renders all sections cleanly.

## Test
`go doc ./src/go/ cmdClose` must include the three-step close semantics.
`go doc ./src/go/ cmdValidate` must list all 13 validation rules.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Every cmdXxx has a full doc comment drawn from the spec
- [ ] Format constants extracted and documented
- [ ] `go doc ./src/go/` output is readable as a reference manual
- [ ] `make test` still passes
